{"track":"tahsili","num":"1.01","slug":"algebra-equations","title":"Algebra & Equations","subtitle":"ClipSAT Printable Practice Suite (clipsat.org) • Topic 1.01 • 20 FRQs + 25 MCQs • Difficulty Progression • Cross-Lesson Synthesis","sections":[{"heading":"Part I — Free-Response Questions (FRQs): Foundational Fluency (1–7)","questions":[{"q":"Solve $2x-5<9$ and graph the solution set on a number line.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Linear inequalities","answer":"$2x<14\\Rightarrow x<7$.","explanation":"$2x<14\\Rightarrow x<7$.","figure":{"type":"numberline","min":3,"max":11,"shade":null,"marks":[{"x":7,"open":true,"label":"7"}],"width":250}},{"q":"Solve $3x-7=11$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Solving linear equations","answer":"$3x=18$, so $x=6$.","explanation":"$3x=18$, so $x=6$.","figure":{"type":"plot","fns":["0.5*(x - (0))**2 + (-1)","0.5*x + 1"],"xmin":-5,"xmax":5,"ymin":-4,"ymax":6,"point_labels":[{"x":0,"y":-1,"label":"$(0,-1)$"}],"width":230}},{"q":"Solve $5(x-2)=3x+4$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Solving linear equations","answer":"$5x-10=3x+4\\Rightarrow2x=14\\Rightarrow x=7$.","explanation":"$5x-10=3x+4\\Rightarrow2x=14\\Rightarrow x=7$."},{"q":"Solve $\\frac{3x-2}{4}=x-1$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Solving linear equations","answer":"$3x-2=4(x-1)=4x-4\\Rightarrow-x=-2\\Rightarrow x=2$.","explanation":"$3x-2=4(x-1)=4x-4\\Rightarrow-x=-2\\Rightarrow x=2$."},{"q":"Solve $2(x+3)-5=3(x-1)$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Solving linear equations","answer":"$2x+1=3x-3\\Rightarrow-x=-4\\Rightarrow x=4$.","explanation":"$2x+1=3x-3\\Rightarrow-x=-4\\Rightarrow x=4$."},{"q":"Expand and simplify $3(2x-1)-2(x-4)$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Expanding and simplifying expressions","answer":"$6x-3-2x+8=4x+5$.","explanation":"$6x-3-2x+8=4x+5$.","figure":{"type":"plot","fns":["0.5*(x - (1))**2 + (-1)","0.5*x + 1"],"xmin":-5,"xmax":5,"ymin":-4,"ymax":6,"point_labels":[{"x":1,"y":-1,"label":"$(1,-1)$"}],"width":230}},{"q":"Expand $(x+5)(x-2)$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Expanding and simplifying expressions","answer":"$x^2-2x+5x-10=x^2+3x-10$.","explanation":"$x^2-2x+5x-10=x^2+3x-10$."}]},{"heading":"Part II — Free-Response Questions (FRQs): Intermediate Multi-Step Application (8–14)","questions":[{"q":"Expand $(2x-3)^2$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Expanding and simplifying expressions","answer":"$(2x-3)^2=4x^2-12x+9$.","explanation":"$(2x-3)^2=4x^2-12x+9$."},{"q":"Simplify $\\frac{6x^2-9x}{3x}$ (for $x\\neq0$).","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Expanding and simplifying expressions","answer":"$\\frac{3x(2x-3)}{3x}=2x-3$.","explanation":"$\\frac{3x(2x-3)}{3x}=2x-3$."},{"q":"Factor $x^2+7x+12$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Factoring quadratic expressions","answer":"$(x+3)(x+4)$.","explanation":"$(x+3)(x+4)$.","figure":{"type":"plot","fns":["0.5*(x - (-1))**2 + (-1)","0.5*x + 1"],"xmin":-5,"xmax":5,"ymin":-4,"ymax":6,"point_labels":[{"x":-1,"y":-1,"label":"$(-1,-1)$"}],"width":230}},{"q":"Factor $x^2-2x-15$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Factoring quadratic expressions","answer":"$(x-5)(x+3)$.","explanation":"$(x-5)(x+3)$."},{"q":"Factor $2x^2+5x-3$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Factoring quadratic expressions","answer":"$(2x-1)(x+3)$.","explanation":"$(2x-1)(x+3)$."},{"q":"Factor $x^2-49$ using the difference of squares.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Factoring quadratic expressions","answer":"$(x-7)(x+7)$.","explanation":"$(x-7)(x+7)$."},{"q":"Solve $x^2-5x+6=0$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Solving quadratic equations by factoring","answer":"$(x-2)(x-3)=0$, so $x=2$ or $x=3$.","explanation":"$(x-2)(x-3)=0$, so $x=2$ or $x=3$."}]},{"heading":"Part III — Free-Response Questions (FRQs): Challenging & Cross-Lesson Synthesis (15–20)","questions":[{"q":"Solve $x^2+2x-8=0$.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Solving quadratic equations by factoring","cross_lesson":"9.01 Statistics & Probability","answer":"$(x+4)(x-2)=0$, so $x=-4$ or $x=2$.","explanation":"$(x+4)(x-2)=0$, so $x=-4$ or $x=2$."},{"q":"Solve $2x^2-5x-3=0$.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Solving quadratic equations by factoring","cross_lesson":"2.01 Functions & Transformations","answer":"$(2x+1)(x-3)=0$, so $x=-\\frac{1}{2}$ or $x=3$.","explanation":"$(2x+1)(x-3)=0$, so $x=-\\frac{1}{2}$ or $x=3$."},{"q":"Solve $x^2-9x+20=0$.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"FRQ","target":"Solving quadratic equations by factoring","cross_lesson":"3.01 Sequences & Series","answer":"$(x-4)(x-5)=0$, so $x=4$ or $x=5$.","explanation":"$(x-4)(x-5)=0$, so $x=4$ or $x=5$."},{"q":"Use the quadratic formula $x=\\frac{-b\\pm\\sqrt{b^2-4ac}}{2a}$ to solve $x^2+3x+1=0$, leaving the answer in exact form.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"FRQ","target":"The quadratic formula and the discriminant","cross_lesson":"4.01 Trigonometry","answer":"$a=1,b=3,c=1$. $x=\\frac{-3\\pm\\sqrt{9-4}}{2}=\\frac{-3\\pm\\sqrt{5}}{2}$.","explanation":"$a=1,b=3,c=1$. $x=\\frac{-3\\pm\\sqrt{9-4}}{2}=\\frac{-3\\pm\\sqrt{5}}{2}$."},{"q":"Find the discriminant of $2x^2-4x+5=0$ and state how many real roots it has.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"FRQ","target":"The quadratic formula and the discriminant","cross_lesson":"5.01 Geometry & Coordinate Geometry","answer":"$\\Delta=(-4)^2-4(2)(5)=16-40=-24$. Since $\\Delta<0$, there are no real roots.","explanation":"$\\Delta=(-4)^2-4(2)(5)=16-40=-24$. Since $\\Delta<0$, there are no real roots."},{"q":"Find the discriminant of $x^2-6x+9=0$ and state how many real roots it has.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"FRQ","target":"The quadratic formula and the discriminant","cross_lesson":"6.01 Limits & Derivatives","answer":"$\\Delta=(-6)^2-4(1)(9)=36-36=0$. Since $\\Delta=0$, there is one repeated real root ($x=3$).","explanation":"$\\Delta=(-6)^2-4(1)(9)=36-36=0$. Since $\\Delta=0$, there is one repeated real root ($x=3$)."}]},{"heading":"Part IV — Multiple-Choice Questions (MCQs): Foundational Concept Mastery (21–28)","questions":[{"q":"The graph shows $y=|x-3|$. At what $x$-value does the graph reach its minimum?","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"MCQ","target":"MCQ — Absolute value equations","choices":["$x=1$","$x=3$","$x=-3$","$x=0$"],"correct":1,"answer":"The vertex of the V-shape (the minimum) is at $x=3$.","explanation":"The vertex of the V-shape (the minimum) is at $x=3$.","figure":{"type":"plot","fns":["abs(x-3)"],"xmin":-1,"xmax":7,"ymin":-1,"ymax":6,"width":230}},{"q":"Solve $3x-7<14$, and identify the graph of its solution set.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"MCQ","target":"MCQ — Linear inequalities","choices":["$x<7$","$x\\geq7$","$x\\leq7$","$x>7$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$3x<21\\Rightarrow x<7$.","explanation":"$3x<21\\Rightarrow x<7$.","figure":{"type":"numberline","min":2,"max":12,"shade":[2,7],"marks":[{"x":7,"open":true,"label":""}],"width":250}},{"q":"Solve $-4x+6\\geq-10$, and identify the graph of its solution set.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"MCQ","target":"MCQ — Linear inequalities","choices":["$x>4$","$x<4$","$x\\leq4$","$x\\geq4$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$-4x\\geq-16$; dividing by $-4$ flips the sign: $x\\leq4$.","explanation":"$-4x\\geq-16$; dividing by $-4$ flips the sign: $x\\leq4$.","figure":{"type":"numberline","min":-1,"max":9,"shade":[-1,4],"marks":[{"x":4,"open":false,"label":""}],"width":250}},{"q":"The graph shows the system $y=x^2-4$, $y=3x$. What are the points of intersection?","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"MCQ","target":"MCQ — Linear-quadratic systems","choices":["$(4,12)$ and $(1,3)$","$(-4,-12)$ and $(1,3)$","$(-1,-3)$ and $(1,3)$","$(4,12)$ and $(-1,-3)$"],"correct":3,"answer":"The curve and line cross at $(-1,-3)$ and $(4,12)$.","explanation":"The curve and line cross at $(-1,-3)$ and $(4,12)$.","figure":{"type":"plot","fns":["x**2-4","3*x"],"xmin":-3,"xmax":5,"ymin":-5,"ymax":14,"width":230}},{"q":"The graph shows the system $y=x^2$, $y=2x+3$. What are the points of intersection?","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"MCQ","target":"MCQ — Linear-quadratic systems","choices":["$(3,9)$ and $(1,1)$","$(-1,1)$ and $(1,1)$","$(-3,9)$ and $(1,1)$","$(3,9)$ and $(-1,1)$"],"correct":3,"answer":"The curve and line cross at $(-1,1)$ and $(3,9)$.","explanation":"The curve and line cross at $(-1,1)$ and $(3,9)$.","figure":{"type":"plot","fns":["x**2","2*x+3"],"xmin":-3,"xmax":4,"ymin":-1,"ymax":10,"width":230}},{"q":"Solve $4x-9=15$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"MCQ","target":"MCQ — Solving linear equations","choices":["$x=6$","$x=-6$","$x=24$","$x=1.5$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$4x=24\\Rightarrow x=6$.","explanation":"$4x=24\\Rightarrow x=6$."},{"q":"Solve $5x+3=2x-9$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"MCQ","target":"MCQ — Solving linear equations","choices":["$x=-2$","$x=2$","$x=4$","$x=-4$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$3x=-12\\Rightarrow x=-4$.","explanation":"$3x=-12\\Rightarrow x=-4$."},{"q":"Factor $x^2+9x+14$.","difficulty":"Foundational","question_type":"MCQ","target":"MCQ — Factoring quadratic expressions","choices":["$(x+2)(x+7)$","$(x-2)(x-7)$","$(x+1)(x+14)$","$(x+14)(x-1)$"],"correct":0,"answer":"Need two numbers multiplying to $14$, adding to $9$: $2,7$.","explanation":"Need two numbers multiplying to $14$, adding to $9$: $2,7$."}]},{"heading":"Part V — Multiple-Choice Questions (MCQs): Intermediate Exam Application (29–37)","questions":[{"q":"Factor $2x^2-x-6$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"MCQ","target":"MCQ — Factoring quadratic expressions","choices":["$(2x+3)(x-2)$","$(2x-3)(x+2)$","$(x+3)(2x-2)$","$(2x+1)(x-6)$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$(2x+3)(x-2)=2x^2-4x+3x-6=2x^2-x-6$.","explanation":"$(2x+3)(x-2)=2x^2-4x+3x-6=2x^2-x-6$."},{"q":"Use the quadratic formula to solve $x^2+5x+2=0$, leaving the answer in surd form.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"MCQ","target":"MCQ — The quadratic formula and the discriminant","choices":["$x=\\frac{5\\pm\\sqrt{17}}{2}$","$x=\\frac{-5\\pm\\sqrt{17}}{4}$","$x=\\frac{-5\\pm\\sqrt{33}}{2}$","$x=\\frac{-5\\pm\\sqrt{17}}{2}$"],"correct":3,"answer":"Discriminant $=25-8=17$; $x=\\frac{-5\\pm\\sqrt{17}}{2}$.","explanation":"Discriminant $=25-8=17$; $x=\\frac{-5\\pm\\sqrt{17}}{2}$."},{"q":"Solve $|3x+2|=13$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"MCQ","target":"MCQ — Absolute value equations","choices":["$x=\\frac{11}{3}$ or $x=5$","$x=5$ or $x=-5$","$x=-\\frac{11}{3}$ or $x=5$","$x=\\frac{11}{3}$ or $x=-5$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$3x+2=13\\Rightarrow x=\\frac{11}{3}$; $3x+2=-13\\Rightarrow x=-5$.","explanation":"$3x+2=13\\Rightarrow x=\\frac{11}{3}$; $3x+2=-13\\Rightarrow x=-5$."},{"q":"Solve $2x+5>-3$ and $x-1<6$ together (both must hold). Find the combined solution set.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"MCQ","target":"MCQ — Linear inequalities","choices":["$x>-4$","$-4<x\\leq7$","$x<7$","$-4<x<7$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$2x+5>-3\\Rightarrow x>-4$; $x-1<6\\Rightarrow x<7$. Together: $-4<x<7$.","explanation":"$2x+5>-3\\Rightarrow x>-4$; $x-1<6\\Rightarrow x<7$. Together: $-4<x<7$."},{"q":"Solve $\\frac{x}{x-3}=4$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"MCQ","target":"MCQ — Rational equations","choices":["$x=12$","$x=-4$","$x=4$","$x=3$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$x=4(x-3)=4x-12\\Rightarrow-3x=-12\\Rightarrow x=4$.","explanation":"$x=4(x-3)=4x-12\\Rightarrow-3x=-12\\Rightarrow x=4$."},{"q":"Solve $\\frac{6}{x}=\\frac{2}{x-4}$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"MCQ","target":"MCQ — Rational equations","choices":["$x=12$","$x=4$","$x=-6$","$x=6$"],"correct":3,"answer":"Cross-multiply: $6(x-4)=2x\\Rightarrow6x-24=2x\\Rightarrow x=6$.","explanation":"Cross-multiply: $6(x-4)=2x\\Rightarrow6x-24=2x\\Rightarrow x=6$."},{"q":"Solve the system $y=x^2-4$, $y=3x$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"MCQ","target":"MCQ — Linear-quadratic systems","choices":["$(-4,-12)$ and $(1,3)$","$(-1,-3)$ and $(1,3)$","$(4,12)$ and $(1,3)$","$(4,12)$ and $(-1,-3)$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$x^2-4=3x\\Rightarrow x^2-3x-4=0\\Rightarrow(x-4)(x+1)=0$: $x=4,y=12$ or $x=-1,y=-3$.","explanation":"$x^2-4=3x\\Rightarrow x^2-3x-4=0\\Rightarrow(x-4)(x+1)=0$: $x=4,y=12$ or $x=-1,y=-3$."},{"q":"Solve $4(x+9)=x+36$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"MCQ","target":"MCQ — Solving quadratic equations by factoring","choices":["$3$","$-2$","$0$","$2$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$4x+36=x+36\\Rightarrow 3x=0\\Rightarrow x=0$.","explanation":"$4x+36=x+36\\Rightarrow 3x=0\\Rightarrow x=0$."},{"q":"Solve $2(x+7)=3x+23$.","difficulty":"Intermediate","question_type":"MCQ","target":"MCQ — The quadratic formula and the discriminant","choices":["$-11$","$-7$","$-9$","$9$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$2x+14=3x+23\\Rightarrow -x=9\\Rightarrow x=-9$.","explanation":"$2x+14=3x+23\\Rightarrow -x=9\\Rightarrow x=-9$."}]},{"heading":"Part VI — Multiple-Choice Questions (MCQs): Challenging & Cross-Lesson Synthesis (38–45)","questions":[{"q":"Solve $5(x-2)=2x-22$.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"MCQ","target":"MCQ — Absolute value equations","choices":["$-2$","$-6$","$4$","$-4$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$5x-10=2x-22\\Rightarrow 3x=-12\\Rightarrow x=-4$.","explanation":"$5x-10=2x-22\\Rightarrow 3x=-12\\Rightarrow x=-4$.","cross_lesson":"4.01 Trigonometry"},{"q":"Solve $2(x+7)=x+10$.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"MCQ","target":"MCQ — Linear inequalities","choices":["$4$","$-2$","$-4$","$-6$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$2x+14=x+10\\Rightarrow x=-4$.","explanation":"$2x+14=x+10\\Rightarrow x=-4$.","cross_lesson":"5.01 Geometry & Coordinate Geometry"},{"q":"Factor $x^2-4x-32$.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"MCQ","target":"MCQ — Systems of linear equations","choices":["$(x-6)(x+4)$","$(x-8)(x+4)$","$(x+8)(x-4)$","$(x-8)(x-2)$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$(x-8)(x+4)$.","explanation":"$(x-8)(x+4)$.","cross_lesson":"6.01 Limits & Derivatives"},{"q":"Factor $x^2+4x-32$.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"MCQ","target":"MCQ — Rational equations","choices":["$(x+8)(x-4)$","$(x+10)(x-4)$","$(x-8)(x+4)$","$(x+8)(x+6)$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$(x+8)(x-4)$.","explanation":"$(x+8)(x-4)$.","cross_lesson":"7.01 Integration & Applications"},{"q":"Factor $x^2-9$.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"MCQ","target":"MCQ — Solving for a variable in a formula","choices":["$(x+3)(x-3)$","$(x-3)(x+3)$","$(x-1)(x+3)$","$(x-3)(x-1)$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$(x-3)(x+3)$.","explanation":"$(x-3)(x+3)$.","cross_lesson":"8.01 Exponentials & Logarithms"},{"q":"Use the quadratic formula to solve $x^2+8x+3=0$, leaving the answer in exact form.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"MCQ","target":"MCQ — Linear-quadratic systems","choices":["$\\frac{-8\\pm\\sqrt{56}}{2}$","$\\frac{8\\pm\\sqrt{52}}{2}$","$\\frac{-8\\pm\\sqrt{52}}{2}$","$\\frac{-8\\pm\\sqrt{48}}{2}$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$a=1,b=8,c=3$. $x=\\frac{-(8)\\pm\\sqrt{64-12}}{2}=\\frac{-8\\pm\\sqrt{52}}{2}$.","explanation":"$a=1,b=8,c=3$. $x=\\frac{-(8)\\pm\\sqrt{64-12}}{2}=\\frac{-8\\pm\\sqrt{52}}{2}$.","cross_lesson":"9.01 Statistics & Probability"},{"q":"Find the discriminant of $3x^2-4x+9=0$ and state how many real roots it has.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"MCQ","target":"MCQ — Word problems: setting up and solving equations","choices":["$92$, no real roots","$-92$, no real roots","$-92$, two distinct real roots","$-92$, one repeated real root"],"correct":1,"answer":"$\\Delta=(-4)^2-4(3)(9)=16-108=-92$. Since $\\Delta<0$, so there are no real roots.","explanation":"$\\Delta=(-4)^2-4(3)(9)=16-108=-92$. Since $\\Delta<0$, so there are no real roots.","cross_lesson":"2.01 Functions & Transformations"},{"q":"Solve $|x-9|=11$.","difficulty":"Challenging","question_type":"MCQ","target":"Free-Response Questions (FRQs): Foundational Fluency (1–7)","choices":["$-2,20$","$22,-2$","$20,0$","$20,-2$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$x-9=11\\Rightarrow x=20$, or $x-9=-11\\Rightarrow x=-2$.","explanation":"$x-9=11\\Rightarrow x=20$, or $x-9=-11\\Rightarrow x=-2$.","cross_lesson":"3.01 Sequences & Series"}]}]}